-- title:
--   Descent of the DVR property from the adic completion
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative Noetherian local ring with maximal ideal $\mathfrak m =$ `maximalIdeal R`, and let $\hat R =$ `AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal R) R` be its $\mathfrak m$-adic completion. Let $S$ be a commutative ring and $e \colon \hat R \xrightarrow{\ \sim\ } S$ a ring isomorphism. Let $Q \subseteq R$ be a prime ideal and $P \subseteq S$ a prime ideal, and assume that the ideal of $S$ generated by the image of $Q$ under the composite $\varphi \colon R \to \hat R \to S$ of the canonical algebra map $R \to \hat R$ with $e$ — that is, $\varphi(Q)S$, the `Ideal.map` of $Q$ along $\varphi$ — is equal to $P$. Assume further that the quotient $S / P$ is a discrete valuation ring. The conclusion is that the quotient $R / Q$ is a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   This is the descent half of the standard comparison between a Noetherian local ring and its completion: the quotient of $R$ by a prime $Q$ is a discrete valuation ring as soon as the extension of $Q$ to the completion (transported along an isomorphism $e$ identifying the completion with a concretely presented ring $S$) is prime with discrete valuation ring quotient. It is applied in the study of integral models of modular curves, where it converts computations in completed local rings into the assertion that a quotient of a stalk is a discrete valuation ring, in particular at supersingular points.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsLocalRing_isDiscreteValuationRing_quotient_of_map_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_eq.lean

